## Repo Docs Initialization

When a repo lacks `harness-docs/` or `AGENTS.md`, generate a complete knowledge base from the actual codebase. Never make up content — only write what you find.

---

### Step 1: Explore the Repository

Before writing a single file, thoroughly explore:

1. Read root structure, README, and manifests (pom.xml, go.mod, package.json, pyproject.toml)
2. Identify tech stack (language, framework, runtime, database, cloud)
3. Identify the product domain — what does this software do?
4. Identify architectural patterns (monolith, microservices, monorepo, layered)
5. Find existing tests, CI config, deployment setup
6. Scan cross-cutting concerns: auth, observability, feature flags, caching
7. Find any existing docs, wikis, inline comments that reveal intent

Use Glob and Grep extensively. Read key source files. Build real understanding before writing.

---

### Step 2: Generate This Structure

```
AGENTS.md                        ← Map/table of contents, max 150 lines
ARCHITECTURE.md                  ← Domain map, package layering rules
harness-docs/
├── design-harness-docs/
│   ├── index.md                 ← Catalogue of design decisions
│   └── core-beliefs.md          ← Agent-first operating principles
├── exec-plans/
│   ├── active/                  ← Placeholder for active plans
│   ├── completed/               ← Placeholder for completed plans
│   └── tech-debt-tracker.md     ← Known technical debt catalogue
├── generated/
│   └── db-schema.md             ← Database schema or API contracts
├── product-specs/
│   ├── index.md                 ← Product features catalogue
│   └── overview.md              ← High-level product description
├── references/
│   └── stack-reference.md       ← Key libraries, versions, usage patterns
├── plans/                       ← Sub-task plan docs (created by coding-instructions)
├── DESIGN.md                    ← Design system / UI patterns (if frontend)
├── LOCAL_DEV.md                 ← Local setup: prerequisites, env vars, services, debug
├── PLANS.md                     ← How to write execution plans
├── PRODUCT_SENSE.md             ← Product values, user personas, north-star metrics
├── QUALITY_SCORE.md             ← Quality grades per domain and known gaps
├── RELIABILITY.md               ← SLOs, SLIs, latency budgets, critical paths
├── SECURITY.md                  ← Auth model, secrets handling, compliance
├── SONAR.md                     ← Quality gate thresholds
├── TEST.md                      ← Testing strategy, framework, coverage targets
└── APP_LEGIBILITY.md            ← Agent scripts, observability stack docs
```

---

### AGENTS.md Rules

- **Max 150 lines** — move extras to `harness-docs/`
- Must include:
  - Repo description (2–3 sentences)
  - Build commands (test, lint, build, boot, coverage)
  - Module map table (module | purpose)
  - Ports table (port | service)
  - Environment variables table
  - Key config paths table
  - Golden rules (5–10 non-negotiable constraints)
  - Links to key docs
- Written for AI agents — structured, terse, no narrative prose
- Cross-link to detailed docs: "See `harness-docs/RELIABILITY.md` for SLO details"

---

### ARCHITECTURE.md Rules

- Module dependency graph (ASCII or Mermaid)
- Layer order: which modules can import which (never import upward)
- Allowed and forbidden dependency directions with one-line rationale
- Known violations documented as tech debt
- Cross-cutting concern patterns (auth, logging, config)

---

### LOCAL_DEV.md Must Include

- Prerequisites: exact runtime versions, CLI tools
- Environment variables: full table with `[SECRET]` markers
- External services: how to run locally (Docker, mock, port-forward)
- Local startup: ordered steps from zero to running app
- `connections.md` reference: how external deps are resolved
- Common debug scenarios: debugger setup, single test run, state reset

### TEST.md Must Include

- Test framework, commands (all tests / single test / with coverage)
- Coverage requirement: **>80% line and branch on new code**
- Test categories: Unit / Integration / E2E — when each is required
- Agent rules: tests alongside code, never after; mock only at system boundaries
- Diff-aware test command: `mvn test -pl <changed-modules>`

### PRODUCT_SENSE.md Must Include

- Product overview and user personas
- Key API endpoints with input/output contracts
- Business rules and edge cases
- Feature flags and their effects
- Sample request/response pairs for key endpoints

### RELIABILITY.md Must Include

- SLOs for latency, availability, error rate
- Critical paths and their timeout budgets
- Hystrix command configurations and circuit breaker thresholds
- Retry policies and backoff strategies

### QUALITY_SCORE.md Must Include

- Current quality grades per module (A-F)
- Known gaps and improvement priorities
- Coverage metrics per module

---

### Constraints

- Never overwrite existing files — read first, incorporate existing content
- Never make up library names, endpoints, or file paths not in the repo
- Use `<!-- TODO: Fill in after human review -->` for unknowns
- Cross-link docs aggressively
- Progressive disclosure: AGENTS.md is the map, harness-docs/ files are the detail
- Every doc must be accurate to the current codebase — verify claims by reading source
